# --- local AI coding-tool state ---------------------------------------------
# Per-developer, not project content. These steer whichever assistant the
# developer runs, and several hold machine-specific paths or credentials
# (.mcp.json, .claude/settings.local.json, .codex/auth.json), so they are
# ignored deliberately: one developer's tool choice should not show up in
# everyone else's status output, nor get committed by accident.
#
# Patterns are unanchored, so they also match inside nested module projects.
#
# AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md are included on purpose even though AGENTS.md is an
# emerging cross-tool convention: the content is XERJ-specific and only means
# something to developers who opted into that tooling. The policy is total: no
# AI-tool configuration is versioned here, including files a tool itself
# considers shareable. `git check-ignore -v <path>` shows which rule bites.
#
# Repeated in performancetrader-workspace, invesdwin-workspace and
# invesdwin-oss because a developer can clone any one of them on its own.

# Claude Code
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
.mcp.json

# OpenAI Codex, and the AGENTS.md convention (Codex, Amp, Devin, Zed, ...)
AGENTS.md
.codex/

# Cursor
.cursor/
.cursorrules
.cursorignore

# Kilo Code, Roo Code, Cline
# Deliberately total. .kilo/kilo.jsonc is a file Kilo Code treats as shareable
# project config (its own .kilo/.gitignore excludes only the rest) and is still
# excluded here — a tool's opinion about what is shareable does not make it
# project content. Same reasoning for every other tool below.
.kilo/
.kilocode/
.kilocodeignore
.roo/
.rooignore
.clinerules/
.clinerules

# GitHub Copilot
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.github/instructions/

# Gemini CLI, Qwen Code, iFlow
GEMINI.md
.gemini/
.geminiignore
QWEN.md
.qwen/
IFLOW.md
.iflow/

# Windsurf
.windsurf/
.windsurfrules
.windsurfignore

# Aider
.aider.conf.yml
.aiderignore

# Continue, Junie (JetBrains), OpenHands, Crush, opencode, Cody, Tabnine, Goose
.continue/
.junie/
.openhands/
.crush/
.opencode/
opencode.json
.cody/
.tabnine/
.goosehints

# --- IDE, unanchored ----------------------------------------------------------
# The entries above are root-anchored, so a nested module project (this repo
# carries ~30 submodule dependencies) still shows its own .idea/ and *.iml.
# These match at any depth.
.idea/
*.iml
